   "source": [
    "# ScholarMatch\n",
    "### Auto-Reviewing Scholarship Applications with Strands Decider 2B and Amazon Bedrock\n",
    "\n",
    "**Agent Experience Hackathon — AWS User Group Madurai Strands Decider kit**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## What is ScholarMatch?\n",
    "\n",
    "Every university scholarship office faces the same bottleneck: staff reading every application by hand, trying to judge whether a student's written reason is genuine financial hardship or just a wishful request.\n",
    "\n",
    "**ScholarMatch automates that first pass.**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Reads the student's free-text reason against the scholarship policy\n",
    "- Asks **Strands Decider 2B** whether it qualifies — returning `eligible`, `needs_review`, or `ineligible` with calibrated confidence\n",
    "- Low-confidence or vague cases are **always escalated to a human reviewer** — the agent never auto-approves when unsure\n",
    "- Deployed on **Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime** (`us-east-1`, Amazon Nova Pro)\n",
    "\n",
    "Decision pattern: `#policy`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Student message\n",
    "      │\n",
    "      ▼\n",
    "  _resolve()  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "  (look up STU-xxx from applications.json, or use raw message text)  │\n",
    "      │                                                              │\n",
    "      ▼                                                              ▼\n",
    "ScholarshipPolicyCheck.check(reason)              tools: get_application()\n",
    "  │  Strands Decider 2B  (#policy)                      record_decision()\n",
    "  │  3 questions in 1 forward pass:\n",
    "  │    eligibility: eligible / needs_review / ineligible\n",
    "  │    genuine:     yes / no\n",
    "  │    financial_need: yes / no\n",
    "  │\n",
    "  ▼\n",
    "decide()  — 7 explicit rules map probabilities → action\n",
    "  │\n",
    "  ▼\n",
    "_explain()  — deterministic template, no LLM call needed\n",
    "  │\n",
    "  ▼\n",
    "_guard_reply()  — safety backstop, ensures reply text matches verdict\n",
    "  │\n",
    "  ▼\n",
    "Response to student  (served by Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Project Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "agent/\n",
    "  AGENT.md          — use case description\n",
    "  agent.py          — HackathonAgent: main chat() entry point\n",
    "  decision.py       — REUSABLE DECISION PATTERN: ScholarshipPolicyCheck (#policy)\n",
    "  tools.py          — Strands @tool functions: get_application, record_decision\n",
    "  data/\n",
    "    applications.json — 14 sample student applications\n",
    "  eval_cases.jsonl  — 26 labelled cases for benchmarking\n",
    "  demo_script.yaml  — turns played in the demo video\n",
    "  features.yaml     — AgentCore Memory / Gateway config\n",
    "\n",
    "decider_kit/        — reusable library (AWS User Group Madurai)\n",
    "demo/               — web UI (./kit demo)\n",
    "deploy/             — AgentCore CDK project (./kit deploy)\n",
    "submission/\n",
    "  bench/            — benchmark charts and results.json\n",
    "  video/demo.mp4    — recorded demo (114 s, AgentCore target)\n",
    "  article/body.md   — article for AWS Builder Center\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Scholarship Policy\n",
    "\n",
    "The policy the decider reads against every application:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SCHOLARSHIP = \"Need-Based Financial Aid Scholarship\"\n",
    "\n",
    "POLICY = (\n",
    "    \"The Need-Based Financial Aid Scholarship supports students who face a genuine, specific \"\n",
    "    \"financial difficulty that affects their ability to pay tuition or to continue studying. A \"\n",
    "    \"qualifying application describes a real, concrete situation - such as loss of a parent's \"\n",
    "    \"income, an unpaid medical bill, a family emergency, or sudden loss of part-time work - with \"\n",
    "    \"enough detail that a reviewer can tell what happened and why aid is needed. Generic requests \"\n",
    "    \"for help (for example 'I need money for college'), reasons that describe academic merit or \"\n",
    "    \"ambition rather than financial need, and reasons that are vague, templated, or clearly \"\n",
    "    \"invented do not qualify. When a reason is borderline or too vague to judge, hold the \"\n",
    "    \"application for human review rather than deciding automatically.\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(POLICY)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Strands Decider 2B Questions\n",
    "\n",
    "Three typed questions asked in **one forward pass** — sharing a single state encoding.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Question | Type | Options |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `eligibility` | `choice` | eligible / needs_review / ineligible |\n",
    "| `genuine` | `noul` (yes/no) | is the reason specific and genuine? |\n",
    "| `financial_need` | `noul` (yes/no) | does it describe real financial hardship? |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# from agent/decision.py\n",
    "from decider_kit import Decider\n",
    "\n",
    "QUESTIONS = {\n",
    "    \"eligibility\": Decider.choice(\n",
    "        f\"Does the applicant's reason match the {SCHOLARSHIP} policy?\\nPolicy: {POLICY}\",\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"eligible\": \"a specific, genuine financial difficulty that clearly affects the \"\n",
    "                        \"applicant's ability to pay tuition or continue studying, matching the policy\",\n",
    "            \"needs_review\": \"the reason is borderline, too vague, or too short to judge with \"\n",
    "                            \"confidence; hold it for a human reviewer\",\n",
    "            \"ineligible\": \"the reason describes academic merit, ambition, a generic wish for \"\n",
    "                          \"money, or otherwise does not match the financial-need policy\",\n",
    "        },\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"genuine\": Decider.noul(\n",
    "        \"Is the applicant's reason specific and genuine, rather than vague, generic, or templated?\",\n",
    "        {\"true\": \"it names a concrete situation with real, specific detail\",\n",
    "         \"false\": \"it is generic, templated, or lacks concrete detail\"},\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"financial_need\": Decider.noul(\n",
    "        \"Does the applicant's reason describe a real financial hardship that affects their ability \"\n",
    "        \"to pay tuition or continue studying?\",\n",
    "        {\"true\": \"it describes loss of income, unpaid bills, a family emergency, or another \"\n",
    "                 \"concrete financial difficulty that prevents the applicant from paying tuition\",\n",
    "         \"false\": \"it describes academic achievement, ambition, a preference, a purchase, \"\n",
    "                  \"or any reason other than a financial difficulty that affects tuition payment\"},\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"QUESTIONS defined:\", list(QUESTIONS.keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Decision Rules\n",
    "\n",
    "The `decide()` function maps the decider's probabilities to a final action using 7 explicit rules. The code never guesses — every case follows a deterministic path:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Rule | Condition | Action |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 0 | Academic merit text, no financial text | `ineligible` |\n",
    "| 1 | Confidence < 0.6 OR genuine < 0.4 | `needs_review` |\n",
    "| 2 | Eligible label, prob_ineligible ≥ 0.30 | `needs_review` |\n",
    "| 3 | Eligible label, genuine < 0.6 | `needs_review` |\n",
    "| 3a | Eligible label, merit text, no financial text | `ineligible` |\n",
    "| 3b | Eligible label, no text signals but financial score high | `needs_review` |\n",
    "| 4 | Eligible label, financial_need < 0.5 | `ineligible` |\n",
    "| 5 | All gates pass | `eligible` |\n",
    "| 6 | Ineligible label | `ineligible` |\n",
    "| 7 | needs_review or unknown | `needs_review` |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
