    "## Reusing the Decision Pattern\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy `agent/decision.py` into your own project and adapt these three things:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# 1. Replace with your policy\n",
    "SCHOLARSHIP = \"Your Scholarship Name\"\n",
    "POLICY = \"Your policy text in plain prose...\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Reword the questions for your domain\n",
    "QUESTIONS = {\n",
    "    \"eligibility\": Decider.choice(\"Does the reason match the policy?\", {...}),\n",
    "    \"genuine\":     Decider.noul(\"Is it specific and genuine?\", {...}),\n",
    "    \"financial_need\": Decider.noul(\"Does it describe real hardship?\", {...}),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Adjust thresholds in decide() to match your tolerance\n",
    "check = ScholarshipPolicyCheck(\n",
    "    decider,\n",
    "    sure=0.6,            # below this confidence → human review\n",
    "    genuine_floor=0.4,   # below this → human review\n",
    "    genuine_eligible=0.6,# must exceed this to reach 'eligible'\n",
    "    financial_floor=0.5, # below this financial_need → ineligible\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Call it before your LLM writes the reply\n",
    "verdict = check.check(applicant_reason)\n",
    "# verdict.action: 'eligible' | 'needs_review' | 'ineligible'\n",
    "# verdict.confidence, verdict.genuine, verdict.financial_need\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Works for any domain where you classify free text against a written policy: content moderation, intake triage, compliance checking, eligibility screening."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Design Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why Strands Decider 2B instead of asking the LLM?**\n",
    "- 4.4× faster at the median (4 s vs 18 s)\n",
    "- Returns calibrated probabilities — the code can branch on a number, not parse text\n",
    "- 100% accuracy on cases it answered confidently (above 0.7 threshold)\n",
    "- Three questions in one forward pass — same latency as one\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why deterministic explanation templates?**\n",
    "- The LLM and the decider can disagree on wording. Templates guarantee the reply always matches the verdict. The `_guard_reply()` backstop catches any remaining drift.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why explicit decision rules instead of trusting the decider label directly?**\n",
    "- The `needs_review` cases (vague reasons) were often labelled `ineligible` by the decider. The rules compensate: low confidence or low genuine score → `needs_review` regardless of the raw label. The decider provides signal; the rules own the policy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Honest weak spots**\n",
    "- `eligibility` question accuracy is 61.5% alone; the rules bring the final action accuracy higher\n",
    "- Decider latency is 4–5 s on the hosted API — a GPU-local deployment would cut this to under 0.3 s\n",
    "- 13 test cases is a small dataset; a larger labelled set would give tighter accuracy estimates\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
